   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 620 of the laws of 1938 incorporating the Volunteer\nand Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association of Millwood, New York, and\nproviding for its powers and duties, and providing for the payment to such\ncorporation of a share of the foreign fire insurance premium taxes, in\nrelation to the purposes and duties of such association and making certain\ntechnical amendments thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S9207",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9207-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Chap 620 of 1938",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Assoc., Inc.",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9207\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 620 of the laws of 1938 incorporating the Volun-\nteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association of Millwood, New York,\nand providing for its powers and duties, and providing for the payment\nto such corporation of a share of the foreign fire insurance premium\ntaxes, in relation to the purposes and duties of such association and\nmaking certain technical amendments thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo incorporate Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association of\nMillwood, New York\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one the Volunteer and Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association of\nMillwood, New York, and providing for its powers and duties.\n\nSection 2 provides that all persons who are now, or have been, or here-\nafter shall be active volunteer members of the Millwood Fire Department\nin the county of Westchester, and who have acquired or shall hereafter\nacquire the status of exempt volunteer fire-fighter as defined in\nsection 200 of the general municipal law by virtue of having rendered\nservice in the Millwood Fire Department, shall be eligible for member-\nship in the corporation created by this act.\n\nSection 3 provides that the powers and duties of the association.\n\nSection 4 provides that the control and disposal of the funds, property\nand estate of the said association, the exercise of its powers, and the\nmanagement and control of its affairs shall be vested in and exercised\nby a board of six trustees.\n\nSection 5 governs the required meetings of the corporation.\n\nSection 6 established termination of membership status under certain\nconditions.\n\nSection 7 governs the situation of a failure to elect officers in a\ntimely manner.\n\nSection 8 Governs the funding source of the association.\n\nSection 9 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York's volunteer fire departments are struggling to recruit and\nretain members at an alarming rate. Creating the Bedford Hills Fire\nDistrict benevolent association will help to allow the Millwood Fire\nDepartment to maintain a capable and enthusiastic volunteer force which\nhas the capabilities to provide relief, aid and assistance to the volun-\nteer members of such corporation and their families who are indigent,\ndisabled or injured in the performance of their duties.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
